  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In the 1980s, someone phoned Space Command, the US military command for space operations, and asked to join a secret programme about an alien threat. The caller was John Brandenburg, a physicist who argues that Mars once had life destroyed by nuclear war, and he tells it himself. He says he told the man who answered, \"I've heard there is an extraterrestrial threat whose existence is classified. I'd like to help with that program,\" and the man replied, \"Oh, okay. Here, let me see if I can connect you with somebody,\" as if such a programme existed."
